{=============================================================================
  Screw compressor from catalogue data (Grasso C-52, R717)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0269
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Isentropic and volumetric effectiveness of an R717 (ammonia) Grasso C-52
  screw compressor computed directly from manufacturer (catalogue) data: the
  24 catalogue rows (condensing/evaporating temperature, capacity, electrical
  power) are read from a lookup table and turned into epsilon_s and epsilon_v
  versus pressure ratio, plus part-load effectiveness at PLF = 0.42.
  Inputs : lookup table (24 rows), fluid$, V_s_cp, rpm_cp, DELTAT_oh,
           DELTAT_sc, PLF, mm; Outputs: epsilon_s_cp_mes[i],
           epsilon_v_cp_mes[i], R_p_cp[i], epsilon_s_pl[i], epsilon_v_pl[i],
           M_dot_cp[i], Q_dot_ev[i]
  Units  : SI - temperatures in °C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : Laborelec compressor toolkit 2002, F. Trebilcock (ULiège) - README.md
============================================================================}

"!MODEL"
"The model obtains the curves of the isentropic and volumetric effectiveness
 directly from the manufacturer information. The catalogue data (compressor
 selection software) go into the lookup table of the model; given the swept
 volume of the compressor, its rotational speed and the superheating at which
 the data were taken, the effectiveness can be plotted versus the pressure
 ratio. As in the original."

n = 24                          "number of rows in the lookup table [-]"
DUPLICATE i = 1, n

"Measured effectiveness"
w_mes[i] = W_dot_cp_mes[i]/M_dot_cp[i]               "measured specific work [J/kg]"
epsilon_s_cp_mes[i] = w_s[i]/w_mes[i]                "global isentropic effectiveness [-]"
V_dot_su_cp_mes[i] = M_dot_cp[i]*v_su_cp[i]          "suction volume flow rate [m^3/s]"
epsilon_v_cp_mes[i] = V_dot_su_cp_mes[i]/V_dot_sw_cp[i]  "global volumetric effectiveness [-]"
w_s[i] = h_exs_cp[i] - h_su_cp[i]                    "isentropic specific work [J/kg]"
" where "
V_dot_sw_cp[i] = V_s_cp*N_cp[i]                      "volume flow rate displaced by the compressor [m^3/s]"
"V_s = swept volume "
N_cp[i] = rpm_cp/60                                  "rotation speed in round per second [1/s]"

R_p_cp[i] = p_ex_cp[i]/p_su_cp[i]                    "pressure ratio [-]"

"Fluid definition:"
h_exs_cp[i] = enthalpy(fluid$, p=p_ex_cp[i], s=s_su_cp[i])  "isentropic exhaust enthalpy [J/kg]"
h_su_cp[i] = enthalpy(fluid$, t=t_su_cp[i], p=p_su_cp[i])   "supply enthalpy [J/kg]"
s_su_cp[i] = entropy(fluid$, t=t_su_cp[i], p=p_su_cp[i])    "supply entropy [J/kg-K]"
v_su_cp[i] = volume(fluid$, t=t_su_cp[i], p=p_su_cp[i])     "supply specific volume [m^3/kg]"

"Outputs measures (manufacturer data)"
W_dot_cp_mes[i] = lookup(i, 4)                       "electrical power [W]"
Q_dot_ev[i] = lookup(i, 3)                           "evaporator capacity [W]"

" Condenser "
h_ex_cd[i] = enthalpy(fluid$, T=T_ex_cd[i], P=P_cd[i])  "condenser outlet enthalpy [J/kg]"
T_ex_cd[i] = T_cd[i] - DELTAT_sc                     "condenser outlet temperature [°C]"

" Evaporator "
h_su_ev[i] = h_ex_cd[i]                              "evaporator inlet enthalpy [J/kg]"
h_ex_ev[i] = h_su_cp[i]                              "evaporator outlet enthalpy [J/kg]"
Q_dot_ev[i] = M_dot_cp[i]*(h_ex_ev[i]-h_su_ev[i])    "evaporator capacity from the cycle balance [W]"

" Properties"
P_cd[i] = PRESSURE(fluid$, T=T_cd[i], X=1)           "condensation pressure [Pa]"
P_ev[i] = PRESSURE(fluid$, T=T_ev[i], X=1)           "evaporation pressure [Pa]"
t_su_cp[i] = T_ev[i] + DELTAT_oh                     "supply temperature [°C]"
p_su_cp[i] = P_ev[i]                                 "supply pressure [Pa]"
p_ex_cp[i] = P_cd[i]                                 "exhaust pressure [Pa]"

"!INPUTS"
"Variable inputs"
T_cd[i] = lookup(i, 1)                               "condensing temperature [°C]"
T_ev[i] = lookup(i, 2)                               "evaporating temperature [°C]"

epsilon_s_pl[i] = epsilon_s_cp_mes[i]*(0.463+1.5255*PLF-1.607*PLF^2+0.62*PLF^3)  "part-load isentropic effectiveness [-]"
epsilon_v_pl[i] = epsilon_v_cp_mes[i]*(PLF^mm)      "part-load volumetric effectiveness [-]"

END

"Constant inputs"
fluid$ = 'R717'                 "refrigerant"
V_s_cp = 0.0013095              "swept volume [m^3] (recommended: use the manufacturer swept volume)"
rpm_cp = 2940                   "rotation speed [rpm] (as in the original; the file name says 2490 rpm)"
DELTAT_oh = 5.001               "superheating [K]"
DELTAT_sc = 0.001               "subcooling [K]"
PLF = 0.42                      "part load factor [-]"
nn = 0.15                       "as in the original (not used in the active equations)"
mm = 1                          "exponent of the part-load volumetric effectiveness [-]"

"Inactive in the active model (as in the original, comments only): the
 commented read of the catalogue mass flow {M_dot_cp_mes[i]=lookup(i,5)} and
 the commented condenser block {h_su_cd[i]=h_ex_cp[i]; Q_dot_cd[i]=...} (an
 alternative condenser balance of an earlier version of the file; it refers to
 h_ex_cp, which no active equation defines). The manufacturer mass flow is an
 output of the active model: M_dot_cp[i] follows from the catalogue capacity
 Q_dot_ev[i] = lookup(i,3) and the evaporator balance.
 Curve-fitting expressions noted in the original (the polynomials it lists for
 this machine at 100 % down to 10 % of the load; the model itself reads the
 catalogue rows from the lookup table):
  100% - epsilon_s_cp_mes[i] = 0.908801447+0.0162294137*(R_p_cp[i]-6.57616267)^2-0.949659513/(R_p_cp[i]-0.317276836)
  ...
  100% - epsilon_v_cp_mes[i] = 0.865229152 - 0.011508488*R_p_cp[i]
  ...
  10%  - epsilon_v_cp_mes[i] = 0.0865478394 - 0.00113186141*R_p_cp[i]
 The full list of the ten polynomial pairs is in README.md."
